        "fileName": "=/home/node/.n8n-files/vault/{{ $binary.data.fileName }}",
        "dataPropertyName": "data",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5041a338-6592-47fe-af38-989bb4cfd3d8",
      "name": "Save note to vault",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.readWriteFile",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        2160,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Folder of PDFs to Markdown notes\nConverts every PDF in a folder to a Markdown note in your Obsidian vault (or any notes folder). Text, headings and tables come through as Markdown, and scanned pages are read with OCR.\n\n### Setup (self-hosted n8n)\nEvery node ships with n8n, so there is nothing to install.\n1. [Get your API key](https://flatmark.dev/go/tpl-folder-to-markdown-notes?to=/app/api-keys). In *Queue the PDF*, create a **Header Auth** credential with the name `X-API-Key` and your key as the value. Pick the same credential in *Check the job* and *Download Markdown*.\n2. Mount your PDF folder at `/home/node/.n8n-files/pdf-inbox` and your vault folder at `/home/node/.n8n-files/vault`, or change both paths. n8n reads and writes files only under `N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO` (default `~/.n8n-files`).\n3. Click **Execute workflow**.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "69cf17af-9a48-47ce-8c42-821a85c3bce8",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How the queue steps work\n*One PDF at a time* hands on the PDFs one after another. *Queue the PDF* sends the file to the flatmark queue. *Check the job* asks for its status every 5 seconds, and *Download Markdown* fetches the result once the job has `succeeded`. A failed job is skipped, and the next PDF goes on.\n\n- Up to 25 MB and 200 pages per file.\n- 10 credits per file, refunded if the job fails. Status checks and downloads are free.\n- Images are not extracted. Keep the PDF in your vault and embed it with `![[file.pdf]]` if you need the figures.\n\nEvery run converts every PDF in the folder, so move converted PDFs out before the next run.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "0e767fc5-8ba6-4e40-9308-72b35078f252",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        700,
        560
      ]
    }
  ],
